Different hypothesis tested
---------------------------
The preserved reconstruction computes the final scale argument in a named float
temporary before calling fn_80120AD0.  Retail instead interleaves preparation of
the integer mask argument, the signed-rank-to-double conversion, and three float
constant loads at offsets 0x474-0x4c4.  This suggested that the original source
may have written the scale calculation directly as the sixth call argument,
allowing MWCC's call-argument scheduler to order those operations differently.

The named scale temporary was removed and the same expression was written
directly as fn_80120AD0's sixth argument.  No compiler flags, ABI declarations,
control flow, or neighboring functions were changed.  The canonical assigned
object was regenerated through configure.py and Ninja.

Measured result
---------------
The direct-expression form still produces an equal-size 1896-byte function and
canonical and relocation-strict scores of 97.49789%.  It remains an honest C
NonMatching reconstruction and is retained as the sole candidate source.

Remaining divergence
--------------------
The instruction diff contains 120 differing rows, predominantly the same
long-lived register-coloring differences: retail/generated output r30/r31,
state r28/r30, object_id r27/r29, is_type_8 r31/r28, and target_state r29/r25.
The conversion/call preparation near 0x474-0x4c4 also remains scheduled
differently.  Both objects contain 81 relocations.  Seventy-eight relocation
sites agree; the three late float constants occur at retail offsets
0x498/0x4a0/0x4ac and reconstructed offsets 0x4a0/0x4ac/0x4bc.

